 structured findings report.\\n\\n{\\\"lens\\\":\\\"SAFETY_BYPASS\\\",\\\"slice\\\":\\\"024B-core\\\",\\\"reviewer\\\":\\\"sonnet-r2-safety_bypass\\\",\\\"round\\\":2,\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"APPROVED_WITH_FINDINGS\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"After fix-rounds 1+2 (closing 1 CRIT + 10 MAJ across all lenses), the SAFETY_BYPASS surface on 024B-core is substantially reduced. Bootstrap-only guard fires exit 1 at line 48-50, before any exit-2 path. Path normalisation via readlink -f / os.path.realpath precedes the denylist; macOS /private/var/* canonicalisation is Darwin-gated and tested. The --patch -- <path> approach for branch_log_modified detection (fix-round-1, closing SAFE-MAJ-002) limits diff scope to the specific log file and eliminates phantom-entry injection via other files; the rename scenario is further blocked by the [ -f \\\\\\\"$BRANCH_PROTECTION_LOG\\\\\\\" ] existence check at line 123, which exits 2 if the log is absent from the working tree. Exactly-one-match assertions on cascade-status (Python re.findall) and log-entry target (parse_entry_repo) resist multi-occurrence and phantom-target injection; test cases 15, 15c, and 17 verify the exact failure modes. Template permissions are confirmed contents:read + statuses:write only; no id-token:write or attestations:write; fork-PR if: clause present and tested in assert_wrapper_contract. Adopter-slug canonicalisation converts jrnb2024/repo.foo_bar to jrnb2024-repo-foo-bar; re.escape(slug) prevents regex injection. SAFE-nit-001 (duplicate chars in parse_entry_repo branch class) and SAFE-nit-002 (missing test for identical unindented duplicate cascade-status lines) are confirmed fixed. Three carry-forward findings from R1 remain open: one MAJ (not applicable carve-out technically unguarded for cohort slices) and two MIN (slug-collision surface undocumented; dispatch-note and status-md accept out-of-repo symlinks). No new findings at CRIT or MAJ level. The open MAJ prevents fixpoint under the 0 CRIT + 0 MAJ criterion.\\\",\\\"findings\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SAFE-MAJ-001\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MAJ\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"Carry-forward from R1, unfixed. cascade-status: not applicable exits 0 with zero enforcement. No technical guard prevents a cohort cascade slice (024C-F) from declaring this value; all three enforcement checks (log-entry present, target-repo match, TF-reference regex) are bypassed. CI exits 0 with a success-class stdout message indistinguishable from a legitimate tooling-slice pass.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"check-invocation-log-entry.sh:144-150 — not applicable branch prints 'OK: ... not a cohort cascade slice — nothing to enforce' and exits 0 before target_repo extraction, branch_log_modified check, or TF-reference validation fire. Verified unchanged vs r3-archive/r1-safety_bypass.json. Test case 15b confirms exit 0 even with STATUS.md and DISPATCH-NOTE carrying other cascade-status artefacts.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"A 024C-F DISPATCH-NOTE declaring cascade-status: not applicable (e.g. copied from 024B-core DISPATCH-NOTE without update) passes CI. enable-required-check.sh invocation-log entry never required; target-repo never verified; TF-reference check never fires. The primary branch-protection audit trail can be silently omitted; single-operator self-review (D-031) is the sole compensating guard.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Add --slice-type cohort|tooling flag to the CLI; reject not applicable when --slice-type cohort is passed. 024B-extras workflow wiring must pass --slice-type cohort for 024C-F jobs. Alternatively require a co-located slice-type: tooling declaration in DISPATCH-NOTE so the parser can enforce exactly-one-tooling-declaration in parallel with exactly-one-cascade-status, making careless copy-paste detectable at CI.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SAFE-MIN-001\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MIN\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"Carry-forward from R1, unfixed. canonicalize_adopter_slug collapses '.', '_', and runs of hyphens to '-', producing identical slugs for repos that differ only in non-alphanumeric separators (e.g. owner/a-b and owner/a.b both yield owner-a-b). A pre-existing TF-024X-renovate row for an earlier adopter falsely satisfies the STATUS.md check for a new adopter whose slug collides.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"check-invocation-log-entry.sh:93-99 — re.sub(r'[^a-z0-9-]+','-',...) merges all non-alphanumeric/non-hyphen chars uniformly. D-044 claims 'adopter-slug canonicalisation per plan-doc spec' without documenting collision exclusion. Current 5-cohort produces no collision; constraint is undocumented and untested for future adopters.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"For the current 5-cohort no collision is exploitable. For future estate expansion a new adopter whose canonical slug matches an onboarded adopter's slug passes onboarded-operator-bump STATUS.md check against the prior adopter's TF row, allowing CI to pass silently without a distinct TF-024X-renovate row for the new adopter.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Document the slug-uniqueness constraint explicitly in D-044 and the canonicalize_adopter_slug function. At adoption time assert the new adopter's canonical slug is absent from existing TF-024X- rows in STATUS.md and branch-protection-log.md. For long-term robustness consider appending a short stable hash suffix to disambiguate structurally similar repo names.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SAFE-MIN-002\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MIN\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"Carry-forward from R1, unfixed. --dispatch-note and --status-md are normalised with os.path.normpath (resolves ./ and ../ segments only, does NOT resolve symlinks), while --branch-protection-log receives os.path.realpath plus an explicit repo-root containment check. A symlink passed as --dispatch-note or --status-md pointing outside the repository is silently followed.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"check-invocation-log-entry.sh:89-95 — normalize_path() calls os.path.normpath. Lines 110-114 apply os.path.realpath + repo-root case check only to BRANCH_PROTECTION_LOG_REAL. No equivalent containment assertion for DISPATCH_NOTE or STATUS_MD. Verified unchanged vs r3-archive/r1-safety_bypass.json.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"An operator passing --status-md pointing via symlink to an external file containing a TF-024X-renovate-<slug> regex match would produce a false-positive pass for onboarded-operator-bump. In practice the TF regex is unlikely to match arbitrary files (fail-closed tendency), but the asymmetric trust treatment is a hardening gap and a minor D-044 trust-model inaccuracy regarding path containment.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Apply os.path.realpath + repo-root containment check to --dispatch-note and --status-md consistently with --branch-protection-log. The REPO_ROOT realpath computation at lines 105-109 is directly reusable; the containment case-pattern and die path already exist for --branch-protection-log and can be copied verbatim for the other two inputs.\\\"}]}\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"759089ba-b128-4f0c-afe6-9f938547f91e\",\"total_cost_usd\":1.2808312499999999,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":10,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":105861,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":518755,\"output_tokens\":48411,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":105861,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":1,\"output_tokens\":20481,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":109769,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":3473,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":3473},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":1886,\"outputTokens\":29,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.0020310000000000003,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000},\"claude-sonnet-4-6\":{\"inputTokens\":10,\"outputTokens\":48411,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":518755,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":105861,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":1.2788002499999997,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"uuid\":\"18c36315-8900-4c98-8342-15c20d65f183\"}\nSTATUS.md:115:| 2 | #98 | **023B** | Per-repo scorecard emitter + schema (closes D-041). NEW `schemas/scorecard-emit.schema.json` v0.1 (MAJOR-pinned per VERSIONING.md D-036). NEW opt-in `scorecard-emit: bool` workflow_call input on `.github/workflows/policy-check.yml` (default false; existing adopters see no behaviour change). New separate `attest-scorecard` job with job-scoped OIDC permissions (closes 023B R1 MAJ-SAFE-001 — workflow-level `id-token: write` would have exposed adopter cloud-IAM trust to ALL runs). 4 fixture pairs (minimal / full / deny-with-waiver / warn-baseline); 12/12 pytest pass. NEVER emits waiver content (invariant 2 enforced by schema + dedicated pytest scan). v1.1.0 → **v1.2.0** (MINOR per VERSIONING.md additive-opt-in). 3-round adversarial review caught 6 unique MAJs. Merged at `5d4341b`; `v1.2.0` tag cut + GitHub release published; release-gate dry-run + post-tag observer both clean. |\nSTATUS.md:118:| 5 | #101 | **023E** | WP-SCP-023 Threshold A scaffolding (closes TF-023D-003 + TF-023A-002; **defers TF-023C-001 → TF-023E-001 + TF-023E-002**). NEW `docs/gates/USER-GATE-D.md` (status: `not-yet-signed`) — 8-criterion checklist for operator sign-off when ≥3 adopters (FLA mandatory) opted in + first weekly aggregator clean. Closed TF-023D-003: `_log_tool_invocation` now reads active key_id from `docs/security/mcp-signing-keys.pub` via new `_resolve_audit_key_id()` helper (graceful fallback `key-ring-unreadable` if key ring empty/malformed; never blocks tool calls). Updated `test_stdio_handshake.py` expected tools list to include `consult_scorecard`. 86/86 MCP tests pass. **fix-round-3:** Two real CI gaps surfaced — (1) SCP-self opt-in attempted then reverted because GitHub blocks `actions/attest-build-provenance` on user-owned private repos (filed TF-023E-001). (2) Wrapper SHA pin bump (v1.0.0 → @5ff2acd) reverted because GitHub Actions validates declared permissions on ALL jobs in a called workflow at startup (BEFORE `if:` evaluation), and the `attest-scorecard` job's `attestations: write` + `id-token: write` exceed the wrapper's ceiling — startup_failure even with `scorecard-emit: false` (filed TF-023E-002 — restructure policy-check.yml so attest-scorecard is a separate top-level workflow file). USER-GATE-D criterion (i) updated: SCP-self carve-out — satisfied set is now `FLA + ≥2 of {PIM / recommender / mapp-doc-agent / control-tower}`. R1/R2 adversarial review missed both constraints (only visible at actual CI runtime in this repo's specific visibility/ownership context). Wrapper stays pinned at v1.0.0 (@41a5299) until TF-023E-002 closes. Merged at `295e0da`. |\nSTATUS.md:119:| 6 | #102 | **024A** | WP-SCP-024 plan-doc v0.1 — estate cascade. Defines adopter cohort `{pim, recommender, shopify-app, mapp-doc-agent, control-tower}` (per D-035) explicitly **FLA-independent** per operator direction; canary-first sequencing PIM → control-tower → mapp-doc-agent + recommender → shopify-app; per-adopter onboarding contract (adopter PR + SCP-side cascade slice + invocation log + post-bake observation window ≥1 calendar week + ≥1 Renovate bump cycle). Reserves D-044/D-045/D-046 for implementation slices 024B/024C/024G. Threshold A: ≥3 of 5 cohort adopters required-check live + ≥1 SCP minor version-bump propagated cleanly via Renovate + USER-GATE-E signed. Required-check cascade is primary deliverable; scorecard-emit opt-in is secondary follow-up gated on TF-023E-002 closure. **Cascade-status spec hardened over 9 review rounds** (32 unique MAJ + 1 CRIT closed across 8 fix-rounds — unprecedented; cause was the cascade-status / CI-enforcement clause being structurally cross-cutting): 3 close-states (`onboarded`, `onboarded-operator-bump`, `blocked-on-adopter-conflict`) × 4 CI behaviours (3 named + fail-closed default) × (positive evidence + machine-enforceable regex format spec + negative assertion). WP-SCP-024 is the natural successor to the 5-move MVCP — turns SCP's estate observability (WP-SCP-023) into action. Merged at `4dc3faa`. |\nSTATUS.md:141:**Operator decision (locked 2026-05-09):** WP-SCP-024 slice 024B split into 024B-core (scaffolder + adopter wrapper template + cascade-status CI enforcement script + tests) + 024B-extras (`--restore` mode + ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass + `.github/workflows/` CI wiring + step 7 operator-interactive demo). Empirical justification: original 024B accumulated 7 fix-rounds + 7 R-rounds with each round closing 5-6 MAJ but introducing 2-3 new defects in just-added code; R6 missed a primary deliverable; R7 fix introduced bootstrap defect on slice's own PR. Surface-area-too-large for single-pass convergence. Split is incremental delivery, NOT descope — both halves still ship; both required before 024C cohort onboarding opens.\nSTATUS.md:147:| 1 | Slice 024B-core: `scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh` + `templates/adopter-wrapper.yml.tmpl` + `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh` (CLI) + `tests/scaffolder/test_scaffold_downstream.sh` + `tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh` (cascade-status enforcement only). D-044 filed scoped to core. Branch: `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-core`. |\nSTATUS.md:233:- **TF-023A-002** (medium priority): Cross-repo notification (v1.2.0 release announcement to ACC / CT / mapp-estate-regression) — **re-deferred to slice 023E** (was 023D; 023D ships exposure surface but Threshold A onboarding is where adopters first participate). Until adopters can opt in with the exposure surface live, the notification is a \"pre-Threshold-A FYI\" only. Filed at WP-SCP-023 023A; re-deferred at 023D R1 completeness CMP-MIN-001.\nSTATUS.md:250:- **TF-023E-002** (medium priority): SCP-self wrapper SHA pin is **stuck at v1.0.0 (@41a5299)** — bumping to any post-WP-SCP-023 SHA produces `startup_failure` because GitHub Actions validates declared permissions on ALL jobs in a called workflow at startup (BEFORE `if:` evaluation) against the caller's ceiling. The `attest-scorecard` job in `policy-check.yml@5ff2acd` declares `attestations: write` + `id-token: write`, which exceeds the wrapper's `contents:read + statuses:write` ceiling, even when `scorecard-emit: false` would skip the job at runtime. Closure path: (a) restructure `policy-check.yml` so `attest-scorecard` lives in a separate top-level workflow file (called workflows can't have job-scoped perms above caller ceiling regardless of `if:`), OR (b) once TF-023E-001 unblocks (repo public/org-owned), grant `attestations: write` + `id-token: write` universally at the wrapper level. (a) preserves least-privilege for opt-out adopters and is the recommended path. Surfaced at 023E fix-round-3 (the bumped wrapper failed startup_failure even after reverting `scorecard-emit: true` because the SHA bump alone trips the validation). Real adopters that opt in MUST follow the (b) path because they will universally grant the two permissions per ADOPT-001 §12.7.15 step 2.\nSTATUS.md:272:- **D-041 (2026-05-03)** — Adopt the cross-repo scorecard data shape (`schemas/scorecard-emit.schema.json` v0.1) + opt-in adopter participation model per WP-SCP-023 023B. MAJOR-pinned schema; default-false `scorecard-emit: bool` workflow_call input; OIDC artifact attestation via `actions/attest-build-provenance@v4.1.0`; aggregator verifies at slice 023C via `gh attestation verify --signer-workflow`. NEVER carries waiver content (invariant 2 enforced by schema's `additionalProperties: false`). v1.1.0 → v1.2.0 (MINOR per VERSIONING.md additive-opt-in). Closes plan-doc §9 D-041 reservation.\nscripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh:5:# Enforces the cascade-status contract defined by WP-SCP-024 plan-doc\nscripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh:7:# diff-base comparison. \"not applicable\" is for tooling slices ONLY\nscripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh:132:matches = re.findall(r'^cascade-status:\\s+([^\\r\\n]+?)\\s*$', text, re.M)\nscripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh:135:    print(f\"ERROR: expected exactly one cascade-status match, found {len(matches)}: {joined}\", file=sys.stderr)\nscripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh:144:  \"not applicable\")\nscripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh:146:    # \"not applicable\" is reserved for tooling slices ONLY; cohort\nscripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh:148:    printf 'OK: DISPATCH-NOTE declares cascade-status: not applicable; not a cohort cascade slice — nothing to enforce\\n'\nscripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh:152:    die \"FAIL-CLOSED: cascade-status field absent or unrecognised; must be one of {onboarded, onboarded-operator-bump, blocked-on-adopter-conflict, not applicable}\"\nscripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh:174:  branch_log_patch=\"$(gh pr diff \"$PR\" --patch -- \"$BRANCH_PROTECTION_LOG_REPO_REL\" 2>/dev/null || true)\"\nscripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh:212:    [ \"$branch_log_modified\" -eq 1 ] || die \"ERROR: branch-protection-log.md was not modified for cascade-status=onboarded\"\nscripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh:214:    printf 'OK: cascade-status=%s; 2 checks passed\\n' \"$cascade_status\"\nscripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh:217:    [ \"$branch_log_modified\" -eq 1 ] || die \"ERROR: branch-protection-log.md was not modified for cascade-status=onboarded-operator-bump\"\nscripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh:230:    printf 'OK: cascade-status=%s; 3 checks passed\\n' \"$cascade_status\"\nscripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh:233:    [ \"$branch_log_modified\" -eq 0 ] || die \"ERROR: branch-protection-log.md was modified for cascade-status=blocked-on-adopter-conflict\"\nscripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh:245:    printf 'OK: cascade-status=%s; 2 checks passed\\n' \"$cascade_status\"\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-core/r1-correctness.json:1:{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"api_error_status\":null,\"duration_ms\":903710,\"duration_api_ms\":904858,\"num_turns\":15,\"result\":\"I now have sufficient context to produce the structured findings report.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\\"lens\\\":\\\"CORRECTNESS\\\",\\\"slice\\\":\\\"024B-core\\\",\\\"reviewer\\\":\\\"sonnet-r1-correctness\\\",\\\"round\\\":1,\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"APPROVED_WITH_FINDINGS\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"The 024B-core implementation is structurally sound across all five in-scope files. The scaffolder's bootstrap guard, arg-validation regex suite, path-traversal guard + readlink-f canonicalization chain, SHA existence check (exit 2) vs HEAD-lineage warn, substitution completeness assertion, and 4-file emission are all correctly ordered and implemented. The adopter-wrapper template has correct permissions (contents:read + statuses:write only), fork-PR if: clause, and Renovate marker immediately before uses:. The CI enforcement script correctly implements all 5 cascade-status paths; the exactly-one cascade-status assertion (re.findall + len check) and exactly-one log-entry assertion (parse_entry_repo len check) resist injection; adopter-slug canonicalization (lowercase, hyphens, re.escape) is correctly applied in both onboarded-operator-bump and blocked-on-adopter-conflict paths. The plan-doc invariant-2 regex (\\\\\\\\S.{19,}) is faithfully implemented in both STATUS.md and DISPATCH-NOTE check branches. Tests cover all 5 cascade-status paths, 6+ worked-example matrix cases, phantom-entry injection (case 17), duplicate cascade-status (cases 15 + 15c), slug canonicalization (case 4h), and --restore-mode coupling is confirmed absent. D-044, STATUS.md chain, and plan-doc §6 amendment are all correctly scoped. Three MAJ findings require remediation before fixpoint: (1) gh pr diff || true in --pr mode silently masks diff errors, creating a false-pass hole for blocked-on-adopter-conflict's negative log assertion; (2) the Darwin denylist test exits via writability-check rather than the /private/var/* denylist entry, leaving the entry untested by any case; (3) the scaffolder generates wrappers with post-v1.2.0 SCP SHAs and scorecard-emit:false that will produce GitHub Actions startup_failure (TF-023E-002), with no scaffolder-level warning to operators.\\\",\\\"findings\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"C-CORR-001\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MAJ\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"In check-invocation-log-entry.sh, the --pr path computes branch_log_patch via 'gh pr diff ... 2>/dev/null || true'. If gh exits non-zero after gh pr view succeeds (transient error, rate-limit, large-diff timeout), branch_log_patch is silently empty, branch_log_modified=0. For blocked-on-adopter-conflict the negative log assertion [ branch_log_modified -eq 0 ] then passes — a false-positive for a slice that DID modify the log file, defeating the key safety check from plan-doc invariant 2.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"check-invocation-log-entry.sh:174 — 'branch_log_patch=\\\\\\\"$(gh pr diff \\\\\\\"$PR\\\\\\\" --patch -- \\\\\\\"$BRANCH_PROTECTION_LOG_REPO_REL\\\\\\\" 2>/dev/null || true)\\\\\\\"'. Contrast with the --diff-base path at line 176 which uses 'if ! ...; then die ... 2; fi', making failures explicit. No test exercises a gh pr diff failure after a successful gh pr view.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"A cascade operator who modifies branch-protection-log.md while declaring cascade-status: blocked-on-adopter-conflict would normally fail CI. A transient gh failure silently suppresses this and allows the PR to pass the log-not-modified check. The plan-doc R3 safety finding (bypass via concurrent invocation + conflict-declaration) depended on this check being reliable.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Remove '|| true'; capture the exit code explicitly. If gh pr diff exits non-zero after gh pr view succeeds, die with a diagnostic distinguishing 'file not in PR' from 'command failed'. Alternatively check that gh pr diff exit code 0 or (exit code 1 with empty output) to distinguish the two cases. Add a test case where the fake-gh pr-diff command exits non-zero to verify the controlled failure path.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"C-CORR-002\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MAJ\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"The Darwin-gated denylist test (--output-dir /var/log on macOS) exits 1 via the writability check at line 138-140 rather than the /private/var/* denylist at line 142-146. After readlink-f resolves /var/log to /private/var/log, the directory exists but is not writable by a normal user, so 'must exist and be writable' fires first. The /private/var/* denylist entry is never reached by any test case; a regression that removed it would go undetected.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh:133-146 — readlink-f canonicalisation precedes the writability check at line 138 (which fires for /private/var/log: exists, not writable) and the denylist at line 142. tests/scaffolder/test_scaffold_downstream.sh:264-272 — the only Darwin-gated test uses /var/log, which resolves to /private/var/log, a directory owned by root and unwritable by the test user. No test creates a writable directory under /private/var and verifies denylist rejection.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"If /private/var or /private/var/* were accidentally removed from the denylist (e.g., during a future denylist-refactoring), the Darwin test would still pass (writability fires for /var/log). A scaffolder invocation with a writable path under /private/var/ (e.g. /var/folders/.../T/custom, which resolves to /private/var/folders/.../T/custom) would succeed on macOS, emitting files into a macOS temp directory that may be purged.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Add a Darwin-specific test that creates a temporary writable directory inside $TMPDIR (which resolves to /private/var/folders/... on macOS) and passes it to the scaffolder via the real /var/folders/... path (without the /private prefix). Verify exit 1 and that the error message names the denylist guard rather than writability. This directly exercises the readlink-f canonicalisation + /private/var/* denylist sequence.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"C-CORR-003\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MAJ\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"The scaffolder generates adopter wrappers with 'contents:read + statuses:write' permissions and the provided SCP SHA. With any post-v1.2.0 SHA (including the current main HEAD used in the test), scorecard-emit:false still causes GitHub Actions startup_failure because the called policy-check.yml declares an attest-scorecard job with attestations:write + id-token:write which GitHub validates against the caller's permission ceiling at workflow startup before evaluating any if: conditions. The scaffolder emits no warning about this constraint; the test uses the current HEAD SHA and validates only YAML syntax, not operational correctness.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"templates/adopter-wrapper.yml.tmpl:9-11 — permissions block is contents:read + statuses:write (correct per DISPATCH-NOTE spec) with no scorecard attestation permissions. .github/workflows/policy-check-wrapper.yml:75 — SCP self-wrapper is pinned to v1.0.0 @41a5299 specifically because of TF-023E-002. STATUS.md TF-023E-002 documents the startup_failure for any post-v1.2.0 SHA regardless of scorecard-emit value. tests/scaffolder/test_scaffold_downstream.sh:7 — SCP_SHA is set to the current HEAD (post-v1.2.0), producing wrappers that would fail startup_failure on GitHub Actions.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"Cascade operators using the scaffolder with the current main HEAD SHA (or any post-v1.2.0 SHA) and the default scorecard-emit:false will generate adopter wrappers that fail CI on GitHub Actions with startup_failure. The cascading adopter cannot onboard via required-check until TF-023E-002 is resolved. The scaffolder implies current HEAD is the correct SHA to use (by warning for non-HEAD SHAs) but the current HEAD is non-functional.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Add a check in the scaffolder that compares the provided SCP SHA against the SHA where the attest-scorecard job was introduced (the WP-SCP-023 023B merge commit). If the SHA is post-introduction and scorecard-emit is false and the wrapper permissions omit attestations:write, emit a labeled warning: 'WARNING: --scp-sha is post-v1.2.0; generated wrapper will hit startup_failure in GitHub Actions until TF-023E-002 is resolved. Use a pre-v1.2.0 SHA or grant attestations:write + id-token:write in the wrapper.' Update the test to use the v1.0.0 SHA (41a5299...) for the primary happy-path test to produce a semantically valid wrapper.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"C-CORR-004\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MIN\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"parse_entry_repo hardcodes a literal em dash (U+2014, — ) in the regex 'r\\\\\\\"^###\\\\\\\\s+.+\\\\\\\\s+—\\\\\\\\s+...\\\\\\\"'. The log entry format produced by enable-required-check.sh is the only source of truth for this separator; that script is in 024B-extras scope. If enable-required-check.sh emits a different separator (en dash, ASCII hyphen, or ' - '), parse_entry_repo returns 0 matches and exits 1, producing a false-fail for onboarded slices with the message 'expected exactly one log entry target match, found 0: []'.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh:190-192 — regex contains literal U+2014. All test fixture log entries (e.g. line 163: '### 2026-05-09T00:00:00Z — jrnb2024/pim@main') use the same em dash, so the tests pass. The log format is not specified in D-044 or the plan-doc invariant 2 regex spec (which only defines the TF reference content format). The coupling between the two scripts is implicit and undocumented.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"If enable-required-check.sh (024B-extras) emits log entries with any separator other than U+2014, onboarded cascade slices fail CI with a misleading 'found 0 matches' error rather than a clear format-mismatch diagnostic. This blocks 024C-F cascade slices until the separator is diagnosed and the constant corrected.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Document the expected log entry format in a shared constant or inline comment in check-invocation-log-entry.sh (e.g. '# format: ### <timestamp> — <owner/repo>@<branch>, em dash U+2014'). Alternatively expose the separator as a named constant (LOG_ENTRY_SEP) so both scripts can be verified consistent. Add a parse_entry_repo test fixture with a non-em-dash separator to verify the diagnostic message.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"C-CORR-005\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MIN\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"The develop-branch variant in test_scaffold_downstream.sh (lines 202-214) does not call validate_manifest, leaving the MANIFEST.json field values (default_branch: develop, scorecard_emit: false) unverified for the develop variant. The master variant at lines 189-201 does call validate_manifest. The omission means a regression where the scaffolder writes 'main' instead of 'develop' in MANIFEST.json would go undetected.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"tests/scaffolder/test_scaffold_downstream.sh:189-201 — master variant calls validate_manifest with 'master' and 'true'. Lines 202-214 — develop variant calls only grep + assert_wrapper_contract + rm; no validate_manifest call. The develop variant also does not assert scorecard_emit in the manifest (which is 'false' for this case).\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"A future scaffolder regression that writes the wrong default_branch into MANIFEST.json for the develop variant (e.g. a sed substitution bug that affects the manifest's default_branch field) would not be caught. The MANIFEST audit trail is a D-044 acceptance criterion; this leaves one variant's audit record unvalidated.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Add 'validate_manifest \\\\\\\"$outdir_develop/MANIFEST.json\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"$outdir_develop\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"$SCP_SHA\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"jrnb2024/test-adopter\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"develop\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"false\\\\\\\"' after the grep assertions for the develop variant, symmetric with the master variant.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"C-CORR-006\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"nit\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"The validate_manifest assertion 'len(payload[\\\\\\\"files\\\\\\\"]) != 3' raises 'manifest.files should list 3 of 4 emitted files (MANIFEST.json does not hash itself)'. The phrase '3 of 4' implies MANIFEST.json is a 4th emitted file counted separately, but the scaffolder stdout says 'emitted 4 files' (wrapper + CODEOWNERS-snippet + CASCADE-PR-BODY + MANIFEST.json). A reader might infer MANIFEST.json is in the 4 AND also hashed somewhere, rather than understanding it is excluded from its own files[] array to avoid circular dependency.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"tests/scaffolder/test_scaffold_downstream.sh:75-76 — assertion comment; scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh:236 — 'printf OK: emitted 4 files under %s; manifest at %s' confirms the count is 4 including the manifest itself. The distinction is subtle but could confuse a future maintainer auditing the SHA256 coverage.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Rephrase to 'manifest.files lists the 3 non-manifest emitted files; MANIFEST.json intentionally excludes itself from its own sha256 entries to avoid circular dependency' or similar.\\\"}]}\\n```\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"44e140ea-e4b5-4806-951b-999df30e8001\",\"total_cost_usd\":1.45887455,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":10,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":142365,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":575246,\"output_tokens\":49992,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":142365,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":1,\"output_tokens\":6943,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":147236,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":2510,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":2510},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":2397,\"outputTokens\":25,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.002522,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000},\"claude-sonnet-4-6\":{\"inputTokens\":10,\"outputTokens\":49992,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":575246,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":142365,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":1.45635255,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"uuid\":\"a4ec1996-dd48-4caa-8c81-f93d04ff5fa3\"}\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:89:| D-041 | 2026-05-03 | Adopt the cross-repo scorecard data shape (`schemas/scorecard-emit.schema.json` v0.1) + opt-in adopter participation model per WP-SCP-023 023B (this PR). The schema defines aggregated per-rule counts (raw_findings, denies, waived, rule_config_disabled), waivers aggregate (active_count, by_rule_id, expiring_within_30d), rule-config aggregate (disabled_rules, expiring_within_30d), repo / ref / commit / scp_version / RFC3339 emitted_at, and a verdict (allow/deny/warn). The schema EXPLICITLY DOES NOT include waiver content (`reason`, `approved_by`, `waiver_id` strings) — invariant 2 of WP-SCP-023 plan-doc binds this. The reusable workflow gains a `scorecard-emit: bool` `workflow_call` input (default false) so existing adopters see no behaviour change; opt-in adopters set `with: scorecard-emit: true`. Schema versioning: MAJOR-pinned per `policies/VERSIONING.md` D-036 + WP-SCP-023 plan-doc §10 Q1 — aggregator drops emits with unknown `schema_version`. Verification: GitHub Actions Artifact Attestation (OIDC-based) via `actions/attest-build-provenance@v4.1.0` (SHA `a2bbfa25...`) at emit time; aggregator verifies via `gh attestation verify --signer-workflow` (per D-042 to be filed at slice 023C). v1.2.0 cut on this slice's merge per VERSIONING.md MINOR category | ACCEPTED | This is the first slice of WP-SCP-023's implementation chain (023A plan-doc landed at PR #97, commit `7075234`, 2026-05-03 R4 fixpoint). The data shape was specified at plan-doc level; this slice ratifies it as code surface. Default-false on the workflow input is the load-bearing safety property: existing adopters cannot have new behaviour spring on them; opt-in is explicit per invariant 4. The waiver-content exclusion (invariant 2) is enforced by the schema's `additionalProperties: false` constraint on every level + the explicit field enumeration. The MAJOR-pinning posture means schema breakage requires v2.0.0 + adopter migration; v0.1 prefix on `schema_version` reflects the freedom to amend until first adopter opts in. Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: aggregator runs on the SCP repo with single-operator identity (D-031); 2026-07-21 quarterly review covers. Identified at WP-SCP-023 023A plan-doc §9 D-041 reservation |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:92:| D-044 | 2026-05-09 | Adopt the WP-SCP-024 slice 024B-core operational contracts for cascade scaffolding. Components: (1) `scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh` (`SCP-073-scaffolder` per WP-SCP-020 §11 follow-up + WP-SCP-021 follow-up `SCP-075-scaffolder-compose`) generates adopter-side artefacts mechanically - bootstrap-only (refuses `CI=true` / `GITHUB_ACTIONS=true` per D-035 symmetry); validates `--scp-sha` against SCP main HEAD lineage (warns if not main HEAD; refuses if non-existent); `--scp-sha` 40-char hex regex; `--default-branch` enum {main, master, develop}; `--scorecard-emit` enum; `--output-dir` writability + path-normalised system-path denylist (incl `/private/var/*` macOS canonicalisation); emits `MANIFEST.json` with SHA256 audit; arguments per plan-doc §5.3. (2) `templates/adopter-wrapper.yml.tmpl` is the canonical adopter wrapper shape per ADOPT-001 §12 with Renovate inline-comment marker `# renovate: datasource=github-tags depName=jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-` enabling auto-bump per plan-doc invariant 8 Threshold A criterion; substitutions `{{DEFAULT_BRANCH}}`, `{{SCP_SHA}}`, `{{SCORECARD_EMIT}}`; least-privilege workflow-level permissions (`contents:read` + `statuses:write` only). (3) `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh` CLI tool implements plan-doc invariant 2 cascade-status CI enforcement: 4 enforcement behaviours (fail-closed default for absent/unrecognised; `onboarded` -> log-entry-modified + target-match; `onboarded-operator-bump` -> log entry + `STATUS.md` `TF-024X-renovate-<slug>` row matching invariant 2 regex literally; `blocked-on-adopter-conflict` -> `DISPATCH-NOTE` `TF-024X-conflict-<adopter>` reference + log file NOT modified) + 5th carve-out for tooling slices (`cascade-status: not applicable` -> exit 0). Regex via `python3 re.search()` (PCRE-style); exactly-one-match assertion (closes multi-occurrence injection bypass); adopter-slug canonicalisation per plan-doc spec. CLI tool only - GitHub Actions workflow wiring (`.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml`) defers to slice 024B-extras alongside `enable-required-check.sh --restore` mode + ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass procedure. D-044 was reserved for slice 024B at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc 024A merge (PR #102, 2026-05-04); after the operator-decided scope-split (SCOPE-CORRECTION-2026-05-09.md), D-044 stays scoped to core deliverables; sibling D-NNN may be reserved at 024B-extras authoring time for the deferred surface (`--restore` + break-glass + workflow wiring). Slice 024B-core ships under documented protocol deviation per feedback_four_tier_dispatch.md note + justify rule (kernel hook lives in ACC repo only; per-repo install pattern is FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 - open). | ACCEPTED | D-044 was reserved at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc 024A merge per the §9 reservation block. The original 024B accumulated 7 fix-rounds + 7 R-rounds against a single branch with each round closing 5-6 MAJ but introducing 2-3 new defects in just-added code (R6 missed primary-deliverable workflow wiring; R7 fix introduced bootstrap defect on slice's own PR). Empirical signal: surface area too large (16 files, ~3500 lines added) for single-pass convergence. Operator decided 2026-05-09 to split 024B into 024B-core (this slice; ~5 files; scaffolder + template + CI enforcement script + tests) + 024B-extras (deferred; `--restore` mode + ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass + `.github/workflows/` CI wiring + step 7 operator-interactive demo). Split is incremental delivery, NOT descope - both halves still ship; both required before 024C cohort onboarding opens. Original 024B work preserved at `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-parking` branch (audit trail: 7 codex-fix-round-N-audit.log files + 7 R-round archive directories incl r8-archive carry-forward findings). Slice 024B-core scope is internally coherent: scaffolder generates adopter artefacts; CI enforcement script (CLI) validates cascade-status declarations; tests cover both. The CLI script can be invoked manually as a stop-gap until 024B-extras wires it into GitHub Actions. Bus-factor-1 acknowledged (D-031); 2026-07-21 quarterly review covers. Identified at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc §9 D-044 reservation |\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:26:cascade-status: onboarded\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:149:  grep -Eq 'not applicable.*tooling slices ONLY|tooling slices.*ONLY' \"$SCRIPT\" || fail \"script missing not-applicable tooling-slice documentation\"\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:154:cascade-status: onboarded\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:169:  run_case \"$repo_dir\" 0 'OK: cascade-status=onboarded; 2 checks passed' ''\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:174:cascade-status: onboarded\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:178:  run_case \"$repo_dir\" 1 '' 'ERROR: branch-protection-log.md was not modified for cascade-status=onboarded'\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:183:cascade-status: onboarded\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:206:cascade-status: onboarded-operator-bump\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:224:  run_case \"$repo_dir\" 0 'OK: cascade-status=onboarded-operator-bump; 3 checks passed' ''\ntests/check