stderr\" || fail \"invalid diff-base did not produce controlled diagnostic\"\n  rm -f \"$invalid_diff_base_stdout\" \"$invalid_diff_base_stderr\"\n\n  repo_dir=\"$TMPDIR/case20\"\n  init_case_repo \"$repo_dir\"\n  cat >\"$repo_dir/DISPATCH-NOTE.md\" <<'EOF'\n  cascade-status: not applicable\ncascade-status: onboarded\n- **Target:** jrnb2024/pim\nEOF\n  cat >\"$repo_dir/docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md\" <<'EOF'\n---\n\n## Invocation log entry\n\n~~~markdown\n### 2026-05-09T00:00:00Z — jrnb2024/pim@main\n\n- **Operator:** @tester\n~~~\nEOF\n  commit_case \"$repo_dir\" \"case 20\"\n  run_case \"$repo_dir\" 0 'OK: cascade-status=onboarded; 2 checks passed' ''\n}\n\nmain\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '120,260p' scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh && printf '\\\\n---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,220p' .github/workflows/policy-check-wrapper.yml && printf '\\\\n---\\\\n' && sed -n '140,240p' STATUS.md && printf '\\\\n---\\\\n' && sed -n '80,120p' docs/DECISIONS.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-core/r1-correctness.json && printf '\\\\n---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,220p' docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-core/r1-safety_bypass.json && printf '\\\\n---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,220p' docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-core/r1-completeness_governance.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-core/r1-correctness.json && printf '\\\\n---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,220p' docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-core/r1-safety_bypass.json && printf '\\\\n---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,220p' docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-core/r1-completeness_governance.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"api_error_status\":null,\"duration_ms\":775847,\"duration_api_ms\":776750,\"num_turns\":15,\"result\":\"I now have sufficient context to produce the structured findings report.\\n\\n{\\\"lens\\\":\\\"SAFETY_BYPASS\\\",\\\"slice\\\":\\\"024B-core\\\",\\\"reviewer\\\":\\\"sonnet-r2-safety_bypass\\\",\\\"round\\\":2,\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"APPROVED_WITH_FINDINGS\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"After fix-rounds 1+2 (closing 1 CRIT + 10 MAJ across all lenses), the SAFETY_BYPASS surface on 024B-core is substantially reduced. Bootstrap-only guard fires exit 1 at line 48-50, before any exit-2 path. Path normalisation via readlink -f / os.path.realpath precedes the denylist; macOS /private/var/* canonicalisation is Darwin-gated and tested. The --patch -- <path> approach for branch_log_modified detection (fix-round-1, closing SAFE-MAJ-002) limits diff scope to the specific log file and eliminates phantom-entry injection via other files; the rename scenario is further blocked by the [ -f \\\\\\\"$BRANCH_PROTECTION_LOG\\\\\\\" ] existence check at line 123, which exits 2 if the log is absent from the working tree. Exactly-one-match assertions on cascade-status (Python re.findall) and log-entry target (parse_entry_repo) resist multi-occurrence and phantom-target injection; test cases 15, 15c, and 17 verify the exact failure modes. Template permissions are confirmed contents:read + statuses:write only; no id-token:write or attestations:write; fork-PR if: clause present and tested in assert_wrapper_contract. Adopter-slug canonicalisation converts jrnb2024/repo.foo_bar to jrnb2024-repo-foo-bar; re.escape(slug) prevents regex injection. SAFE-nit-001 (duplicate chars in parse_entry_repo branch class) and SAFE-nit-002 (missing test for identical unindented duplicate cascade-status lines) are confirmed fixed. Three carry-forward findings from R1 remain open: one MAJ (not applicable carve-out technically unguarded for cohort slices) and two MIN (slug-collision surface undocumented; dispatch-note and status-md accept out-of-repo symlinks). No new findings at CRIT or MAJ level. The open MAJ prevents fixpoint under the 0 CRIT + 0 MAJ criterion.\\\",\\\"findings\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SAFE-MAJ-001\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MAJ\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"Carry-forward from R1, unfixed. cascade-status: not applicable exits 0 with zero enforcement. No technical guard prevents a cohort cascade slice (024C-F) from declaring this value; all three enforcement checks (log-entry present, target-repo match, TF-reference regex) are bypassed. CI exits 0 with a success-class stdout message indistinguishable from a legitimate tooling-slice pass.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"check-invocation-log-entry.sh:144-150 — not applicable branch prints 'OK: ... not a cohort cascade slice — nothing to enforce' and exits 0 before target_repo extraction, branch_log_modified check, or TF-reference validation fire. Verified unchanged vs r3-archive/r1-safety_bypass.json. Test case 15b confirms exit 0 even with STATUS.md and DISPATCH-NOTE carrying other cascade-status artefacts.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"A 024C-F DISPATCH-NOTE declaring cascade-status: not applicable (e.g. copied from 024B-core DISPATCH-NOTE without update) passes CI. enable-required-check.sh invocation-log entry never required; target-repo never verified; TF-reference check never fires. The primary branch-protection audit trail can be silently omitted; single-operator self-review (D-031) is the sole compensating guard.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Add --slice-type cohort|tooling flag to the CLI; reject not applicable when --slice-type cohort is passed. 024B-extras workflow wiring must pass --slice-type cohort for 024C-F jobs. Alternatively require a co-located slice-type: tooling declaration in DISPATCH-NOTE so the parser can enforce exactly-one-tooling-declaration in parallel with exactly-one-cascade-status, making careless copy-paste detectable at CI.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SAFE-MIN-001\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MIN\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"Carry-forward from R1, unfixed. canonicalize_adopter_slug collapses '.', '_', and runs of hyphens to '-', producing identical slugs for repos that differ only in non-alphanumeric separators (e.g. owner/a-b and owner/a.b both yield owner-a-b). A pre-existing TF-024X-renovate row for an earlier adopter falsely satisfies the STATUS.md check for a new adopter whose slug collides.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"check-invocation-log-entry.sh:93-99 — re.sub(r'[^a-z0-9-]+','-',...) merges all non-alphanumeric/non-hyphen chars uniformly. D-044 claims 'adopter-slug canonicalisation per plan-doc spec' without documenting collision exclusion. Current 5-cohort produces no collision; constraint is undocumented and untested for future adopters.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"For the current 5-cohort no collision is exploitable. For future estate expansion a new adopter whose canonical slug matches an onboarded adopter's slug passes onboarded-operator-bump STATUS.md check against the prior adopter's TF row, allowing CI to pass silently without a distinct TF-024X-renovate row for the new adopter.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Document the slug-uniqueness constraint explicitly in D-044 and the canonicalize_adopter_slug function. At adoption time assert the new adopter's canonical slug is absent from existing TF-024X- rows in STATUS.md and branch-protection-log.md. For long-term robustness consider appending a short stable hash suffix to disambiguate structurally similar repo names.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SAFE-MIN-002\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MIN\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"Carry-forward from R1, unfixed. --dispatch-note and --status-md are normalised with os.path.normpath (resolves ./ and ../ segments only, does NOT resolve symlinks), while --branch-protection-log receives os.path.realpath plus an explicit repo-root containment check. A symlink passed as --dispatch-note or --status-md pointing outside the repository is silently followed.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"check-invocation-log-entry.sh:89-95 — normalize_path() calls os.path.normpath. Lines 110-114 apply os.path.realpath + repo-root case check only to BRANCH_PROTECTION_LOG_REAL. No equivalent containment assertion for DISPATCH_NOTE or STATUS_MD. Verified unchanged vs r3-archive/r1-safety_bypass.json.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"An operator passing --status-md pointing via symlink to an external file containing a TF-024X-renovate-<slug> regex match would produce a false-positive pass for onboarded-operator-bump. In practice the TF regex is unlikely to match arbitrary files (fail-closed tendency), but the asymmetric trust treatment is a hardening gap and a minor D-044 trust-model inaccuracy regarding path containment.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Apply os.path.realpath + repo-root containment check to --dispatch-note and --status-md consistently with --branch-protection-log. The REPO_ROOT realpath computation at lines 105-109 is directly reusable; the containment case-pattern and die path already exist for --branch-protection-log and can be copied verbatim for the other two inputs.\\\"}]}\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"759089ba-b128-4f0c-afe6-9f938547f91e\",\"total_cost_usd\":1.2808312499999999,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":10,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":105861,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":518755,\"output_tokens\":48411,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":105861,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":1,\"output_tokens\":20481,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":109769,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":3473,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":3473},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":1886,\"outputTokens\":29,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.0020310000000000003,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000},\"claude-sonnet-4-6\":{\"inputTokens\":10,\"outputTokens\":48411,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":518755,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":105861,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":1.2788002499999997,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"uuid\":\"18c36315-8900-4c98-8342-15c20d65f183\"}\n\n---\n{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"api_error_status\":null,\"duration_ms\":640610,\"duration_api_ms\":641588,\"num_turns\":27,\"result\":\"I have all the data I need. Here is the R3 COMPLETENESS_GOVERNANCE review result:\\n\\n{\\\"review_id\\\":\\\"r3-completeness_governance\\\",\\\"slice\\\":\\\"WP-SCP-024/024B-core\\\",\\\"lens\\\":\\\"completeness_governance\\\",\\\"reviewer\\\":\\\"sonnet-r3-completeness_governance\\\",\\\"date\\\":\\\"2026-05-09\\\",\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"APPROVED_WITH_FINDINGS\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"024B-core completeness governance reaches fixpoint on this lens at R3 — 0 CRIT, 0 MAJ, 3 MIN, 2 nit. The round-previous MAJ (cascade-status backtick wrapping causing parse zero-match) and two MINs (conflict-path negative TF-format tests; validate_manifest scorecard_emit:true coverage) were correctly closed in fix-round-2. Core governance posture is sound: SCOPE-CORRECTION-2026-05-09.md delivers the R6→R7→R8 trajectory table, 3 structural problems, explicit incremental-delivery not-descope framing, and extras-parking audit trail. D-044 is filed ACCEPTED scoped to core deliverables and cites SCOPE-CORRECTION by name. Plan-doc §6 split note correctly gates 024C on both halves plus FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001. DISPATCH-NOTE cascade-status field is now a bare line-start value (MAJ from previous round closed). All plan-doc invariants 1–10 have coverage across the delivered files within core scope; extras-only carve-out (--restore, break-glass, workflow wiring) is clean across all 5 files. Anti-descoping is preserved. VERSIONING.md alignment clean — all three deliverables are internal-only under §Scope. Three MINs and two nits carry forward: template silent on scorecard-emit:true permission gap; stale invocation-log-convention language in the DECISIONS.md reservation header; STATUS.md row 3 description ambiguity around FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 retention; 024C AC row missing prerequisites annotation; stale DISPATCH-NOTE status line. All are one-line fixes; none block fixpoint on this lens.\\\",\\\"findings\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"CG-MIN-001\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MIN\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"adopter-wrapper.yml.tmpl is silent on the additional permissions required when scorecard-emit:true is passed. The template emits only contents:read + statuses:write at workflow level regardless of {{SCORECARD_EMIT}}. TF-023E-002 documents that attestations:write + id-token:write are required for the attest-scorecard job, but an operator running the scaffolder with --scorecard-emit true receives a syntactically valid wrapper that produces startup_failure in CI with no in-file indication of why.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"templates/adopter-wrapper.yml.tmpl lines 9-11: permissions block is unconditional (contents:read + statuses:write only). DISPATCH-NOTE scope table: 'opt-in adopters add attestations:write + id-token:write per ADOPT-001 §12.7.15 step 2'. TF-023E-002 in STATUS.md documents the startup_failure mechanism. Template carries no comment on the scorecard-emit:true permission dependency.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"Silent foot-gun for cascade operators using --scorecard-emit true. The scaffolder exits OK; the adopter's first CI run fails at startup_failure. The root cause is not diagnosable from the wrapper file alone without cross-referencing ADOPT-001 §12.7.15 and TF-023E-002.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Add a conditional inline comment in the template adjacent to the permissions block: e.g. '# scorecard-emit: true additionally requires attestations: write + id-token: write per ADOPT-001 §12.7.15 step 2 (TF-023E-002). Add these at workflow level before enabling.' One comment block; does not change emitted YAML for scorecard-emit:false adopters.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"CG-MIN-002\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MIN\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"DECISIONS.md D-044 reservation header note (lines 29-33) retains the original §9 reservation language 'invocation-log convention extension' which does not match the actual D-044 scope. The filed D-044 row ratifies (1) scaffold-downstream.sh operational contract, (2) adopter-wrapper.yml.tmpl, and (3) check-invocation-log-entry.sh CLI — not 'scaffolder writes a rendered-template log entry alongside enable-required-check.sh branch-protection log' as the header implies.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"docs/DECISIONS.md lines 30-32: 'D-044 was reserved for WP-SCP-024 slice 024B (scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh = SCP-073-scaffolder operational contract + adopter-template versioning + invocation-log convention extension).' Filed D-044 rationale (line ~92): check-invocation-log-entry.sh CLI; MANIFEST.json SHA256 audit. Plan-doc §5.3: 'emits a manifest file MANIFEST.json listing every file emitted + its SHA256 for audit' — no branch-protection-log write from the scaffolder.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"Operators reading the reservation header before the filed D-044 row expect a scaffolder-to-branch-protection-log write path that does not exist. Risk of 024B-extras authoring or future adopter onboarding assuming this write happens automatically. No AC dropped (plan-doc §5.3 is authoritative); documentation inconsistency only.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Update the D-044 reservation header note to replace 'invocation-log convention extension' with the actual scope: 'cascade-status CI enforcement script (CLI) — check-invocation-log-entry.sh; MANIFEST.json SHA256 audit emitted to output directory.' One sentence replacement.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"CG-MIN-003\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MIN\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"STATUS.md today's chain PM row 3 states '024C entry now conditional on BOTH 024B-core + 024B-extras merged (was: 024B + FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 closure)' without explicitly naming FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 as a retained gate condition. The parenthetical frames FUP as part of the old state only; a reader relying on STATUS.md could treat it as superseded.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"STATUS.md line 149: 'Plan-doc §6 amendment: 024C entry now conditional on BOTH 024B-core + 024B-extras merged (was: 024B + FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 closure). Cohort cascade gate unchanged in posture; precondition list extended for clarity.' docs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md line 213: '024C remains gated on both halves merging, plus FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 closure, before cohort onboarding opens.' Plan-doc is authoritative and correctly retains FUP; STATUS.md summary is ambiguous.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"A 024C opener reading STATUS.md for current gate conditions could treat FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 as retired and open the cascade prematurely. STATUS.md is the primary operator-skim doc; the 'unchanged in posture' qualifier is easy to miss under time pressure.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Amend STATUS.md row 3 to read: '024C now gated on: (1) 024B-core merged, (2) 024B-extras merged, (3) FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 closed (retained from pre-split gate).' Removes ambiguity without changing the underlying gate posture.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"CG-nit-001\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"nit\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"Plan-doc §6 024C table row acceptance criteria does not inline the split-introduced prerequisites (both halves + FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001). The conditions are in the adjacent 024B split note but not in the 024C AC cell itself, requiring cross-referencing two locations to determine 024C's full gate.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"docs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md line 207 (024C AC column): 'PIM policy-check / scp/policy-check required-check live; ≥1 Renovate-bump-propagation cycle merged clean; D-045 filed.' Split note at line 213 carries both prerequisites. AC column has no prerequisites annotation.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"Cosmetic; correct gate information is one paragraph away. A fast reader of only the 024C row risks missing the FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 prerequisite before opening the slice.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Prepend a Prerequisites line to the 024C AC column: 'Prerequisites: 024B-core + 024B-extras merged + FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 closed (per split note).' One-line addition to the table cell.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"CG-nit-002\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"nit\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"DISPATCH-NOTE Status line (final line) reads 'DRAFT v0.1 — awaiting Codex T3 surgical-clean dispatch' although Phase 1 Codex work completed, two fix-rounds have run, and the slice is in R3 review.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-core/DISPATCH-NOTE.md final line: '**Status:** DRAFT v0.1 — awaiting Codex T3 surgical-clean dispatch.' Recent commits: 'fix-round-2: 0 CRIT + 5 MAJ closed'; 'fix-round-1: 1 CRIT + 5 MAJ closed'. Phase 0 in Sequencing table is marked 'done'; Phase 1 Codex work produced the delivered files.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"Cosmetic; misleads reviewers about the current phase on a first read.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Update Status line to e.g. 'R3 review in progress (2026-05-09); 0 CRIT + 0 MAJ across 2 fix-rounds.'}]}\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"ca228667-9273-4989-823d-cd33e9096908\",\"total_cost_usd\":1.5219984500000003,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":5616,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":147949,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":1418349,\"output_tokens\":34881,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":147949,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":1,\"output_tokens\":4343,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":144195,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":2426,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":2426},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":1482,\"outputTokens\":28,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.001622,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000},\"claude-sonnet-4-6\":{\"inputTokens\":5616,\"outputTokens\":34881,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":1418349,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":147949,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":1.5203764500000003,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"uuid\":\"1f102118-bc29-465d-b567-d0addb5913bd\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '120,260p' scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh && printf '\\\\n---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,220p' .github/workflows/policy-check-wrapper.yml && printf '\\\\n---\\\\n' && sed -n '140,240p' STATUS.md && printf '\\\\n---\\\\n' && sed -n '80,120p' docs/DECISIONS.md\"","aggregated_output":"\n---\n\n**Operator decision (locked 2026-05-09):** WP-SCP-024 slice 024B split into 024B-core (scaffolder + adopter wrapper template + cascade-status CI enforcement script + tests) + 024B-extras (`--restore` mode + ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass + `.github/workflows/` CI wiring + step 7 operator-interactive demo). Empirical justification: original 024B accumulated 7 fix-rounds + 7 R-rounds with each round closing 5-6 MAJ but introducing 2-3 new defects in just-added code; R6 missed a primary deliverable; R7 fix introduced bootstrap defect on slice's own PR. Surface-area-too-large for single-pass convergence. Split is incremental delivery, NOT descope — both halves still ship; both required before 024C cohort onboarding opens.\n\nOriginal 024B work preserved at branch `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-parking` (pushed to origin 2026-05-09; audit trail intact: 7 codex-fix-round-N-audit.log + 7 R-round archive dirs).\n\n| # | Outcome |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Slice 024B-core: `scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh` + `templates/adopter-wrapper.yml.tmpl` + `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh` (CLI) + `tests/scaffolder/test_scaffold_downstream.sh` + `tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh` (cascade-status enforcement only). D-044 filed scoped to core. Branch: `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-core`. |\n| 2 | Slice 024B-extras: deferred. Scope: `enable-required-check.sh --restore` mode + ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass + `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` + step 7 operator-interactive `--restore` round-trip demo. To be branched from merged 024B-core. R8-CORR-001/002/003 (extras-parking r8-archive) carry forward as known findings. |\n| 3 | Plan-doc §6 amendment: 024C entry now conditional on BOTH 024B-core + 024B-extras merged (was: 024B + FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 closure). Cohort cascade gate unchanged in posture; precondition list extended for clarity. |\n\n## Open PRs (post-Threshold-A session close-out)\n\n- **PR #59** 🔄 OPEN (DO-NOT-MERGE) — `canary/deliberate-violation-pre`; permanent fixture; CI=FAIL by design (deny); blocked structurally by required-check.\n- **PR #67** 🔄 OPEN (DO-NOT-MERGE) — `canary/waived-violation`; permanent fixture; CI=PASS via waiver suppression; label-only protection (TF-020H4-002 covers).\n- **PR #81** 🔄 OPEN (DO-NOT-MERGE) — `canary/rule-config-disabled`; permanent fixture; CI=PASS via rule-config suppression; label-only protection (TF-020H4-002 covers).\n- **Dependabot PRs**: ✅ all 4 stale MAJOR-version Action bumps cleared 2026-05-02. setup-python (#72), upload-artifact (#44), download-artifact (#42), checkout (#43) — all merged after CI-green verification on rebased branches.\n\n## Open scheduled follow-ups\n\n| Item | Date | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| D-021 atomic workday filing (D-021 reservation) | 2026-05-31 | docs/DECISIONS.md header |\n| Phase 2 X-CT-Timestamp activation notice (60-day advance) | 2026-07-02 | project_scheduled_followups.md item 3 |\n| WP-SCP-019 D-019 mode.bearer_legacy operational close | 2026-09-30 | project_d019_option_b_slide |\n| 2026-07-21 quarterly review covers TWO independent items: (1) WP-SCP-020 020K bus-factor-1 escalation (CODEOWNERS / break-glass); (2) TF-020G-001 (interactive-confirm review on adopter helper). Both items reach the same date by separate paths but are evaluated independently. | 2026-07-21 | docs/plans/WP-SCP-020-policy-federation-primitive.md §8 + docs/reviews/WP-SCP-022/dispatches/020g/DISPATCH-NOTE.md |\n| Branch-protection quarterly review (bus-factor-1; covers `v*` ruleset, `main` protection, AND `renovate/v*` ruleset) | 2026-07-30 | docs/security/branch-protection.md |\n| WP-SCP-023 Threshold A operator sign-off — `docs/gates/USER-GATE-D.md` lands as `not-yet-signed` at slice 023E; signs when ≥3 adopters opted in + ≥1 weekly aggregator clean. Operator-driven; no fixed date. | tbd | docs/gates/USER-GATE-D.md |\n\n## Tracked-forward items from 020C.1\n\n- ~~**TF-005**: structural enforcement of expired rule-config at release-tag time~~ ✅ **closed in slice 020H.3** (this PR's branch); `.github/workflows/release-gate.yml` refuses a tag-cut when `.scp/rule-config.yaml` (SCP-self) has any `disable: true` entry with `expires_at < <tag-cut date>`. Adopter-side rule-config expiry is enforced separately at PR time via SCP-E007.\n- ~~**TF-006**~~ ✅ **closed in slice 020Q** (this PR) — `tests/conflict_gate/test_conflict_gate.py` gains Python-side mirrors of `policies/scp_common.rego` suppression helpers (`_scp_active_waiver_for`, `_scp_waiver_expired`, `_scp_rule_config_disabled`, `_parse_dateish_ns`); `_run_opa` detects sibling `waivers.json` + `.scp/rule-config.yaml` and passes via `--data`; 5 new fixtures land — SCP-R-001/{waiver-suppressed, waiver-expired, rule-config-disabled} + SCP-R-002/waiver-suppressed + SCP-R-004/waiver-suppressed. All 11 fixtures pass; both engines agree on every code path. Finding-id-level matching deferred to WP-SCP-023 per scp_common.rego comment. Closes the WP-SCP-023 prerequisite gate.\n- **TF-007**: re-tighten `gh attestation verify` to hard-fail when OPA upstream begins publishing Sigstore attestations. **Extended in 020H.2** to also wire a Regal Sigstore soft-warn at re-tightening time — Regal is published via OPA's pipeline and almost certainly shares the same upstream attestation gap timeline; symmetric treatment when the gap closes. Conftest also covered (no published attestations either).\n- **TF-008**: path-scope SCP-R-002 to waivers.json files only (currently narrowed to null/string-rooted detection only) → v1.1.\n\n## Tracked-forward items from 020D1 (closed in 020H part 3)\n\n- **TF-D1-001**: WP-SCP-020 §4 020H part 3 canonical adopter template repo name uses trailing dash (`standards-control-plane-`) — ✅ closed in **020H part 3** (this PR's branch); §12.7.1 + §12.7.2 use the correct repo name.\n- **TF-D1-002**: Document fork-PR refusal as mandatory or optional for adopters — ✅ closed in **020H part 3**; §12.7.1 documents the `if:` as **mandatory** with security rationale.\n- **TF-D1-003**: Wrapper header references 'ADOPT-001 §12' federation appendix — ✅ closed in **020H part 3**; §12.7 federation-primitive adopter integration appendix now exists.\n\n## Tracked-forward items from 020H part 3\n\n- **TF-020H3-001**: Regal binary SHA256 verification — ✅ **closed in slice 020H.2 (this PR's branch)** before the 2026-05-14 deadline. `scripts/.tool-versions` now pins `regal 0.40.0`; `scripts/scp-policy-check.lock` carries Regal SHA256 entries for all four platforms (linux-x64, linux-arm64, darwin-arm64, darwin-x64); `.github/workflows/policy-check.yml` reads `REGAL_VERSION` from tool-versions, `REGAL_SHA256` from the lockfile, and resolves Regal via the new `resolve_regal()` helper symmetric with `resolve_opa()` (vendor-fallback parity). Sigstore attestation soft-warn for Regal not added (folds into TF-007).\n- **TF-020H3-002**: ADOPT-001 §12.7 lacks an explicit \"do these in this order\" adopter onboarding sequence (was R1 completeness COMP-MIN-001). Document order implicitly encodes §12.7.1 → §12.7.2 → §12.7.3 → §12.7.4 setup flow, but a v1.1 §12.7 preamble would make the sequence explicit. No deadline (cosmetic).\n- ~~**TF-020H3-003**: Plan §4 020H part 3 canonical YAML wrapper text uses `standards-control-plane` (no trailing dash) in two places~~ ✅ **closed opportunistically in slice 020M** (this PR's branch). Slice 020M is a plan-touch slice (it amends `docs/plans/WP-SCP-020-policy-federation-primitive.md` for the typo fix itself), satisfying the TF-020H3-003 closure path. **All three lines corrected** across **two logical locations** in the plan: (1) §4 020F `extends:` shorthand `github>jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-//renovate/default#<tag>` (trailing dash added in 1 line); (2) §4 020H part 3 canonical YAML wrapper renovate marker `# renovate: datasource=github-tags depName=jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-` (trailing dash added in 1 line) + reusable-workflow ref `uses: jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-/.github/workflows/policy-check.yml@<commit-SHA>` (trailing dash added in 1 line). The TF's original phrasing \"in two places\" referred to the two logical locations (020F + 020H part 3); the actual character-count is three line-edits.\n- **TF-020H3-004**: §12.7.4 path examples (`services.yml`, `output/findings/waivers.json`, `policies/**`) are SCP-internal naming (was R1 completeness COMP-NIT-001). Estate-cascade adopters (FLA, PIM, recommender, shopify-app, mapp-doc-agent, control-tower per WP-SCP-024) may have different file-shape conventions; v1.1 §12.7 wording could generalise. No deadline (cosmetic).\n- **TF-020H3-005**: §12.7.2 doesn't include a one-sentence rationale for why `renovate/v*` is independent of the federation-primitive `v*` tag series (was R1 completeness COMP-NIT-002). Closure: v1.1 ADOPT-001 maintenance pass. No deadline (cosmetic).\n\n## Tracked-forward items from 020H.1\n\n- ~~**TF-020H1-001**: `enforce_release_gate` workflow~~ ✅ **closed in slice 020H.3** (this PR's branch); `.github/workflows/release-gate.yml` reads `policies/deprecations.yaml` (validated against `schemas/deprecations.schema.json`) and refuses a tag-cut on `push: tags: ['v*']` when any entry's `target_release` matches the candidate AND `announced_release` is not at least one MINOR behind. `workflow_dispatch:` with `dry_run_tag` input lets the operator test before pushing. Annotation: `SCP-EREL-001`.\n- **TF-020H1-002**: `canary-replay.yml` paging rotation — at v1.0.0 the auto-opened `rule-regression` issue assigns `@jrnb2024` only (single-operator per D-031). For estate cascade (WP-SCP-024) a paging rotation would replace the assignee-only signal. Closure path: revisit at WP-SCP-024 planning OR at the 2026-07-21 quarterly bus-factor review when a second maintainer onboards. No deadline (forward-compat). Filed at 020H.1 R1 completeness COMP-MAJ-002 closure.\n- **TF-020H1-003**: `auto-defer` GitHub Action for stale rule-proposals — currently a manual close + `defer` label step (per `docs/reviews/rule-proposals/README.md` §Process step 2). For estate scale (post-WP-SCP-024 cascade) when proposal volume warrants automation, a scheduled GH Action would close PRs with no approvals after the 48h window. No deadline (forward-compat). Filed at 020H.1 R1 completeness COMP-MIN-004 closure.\n- ~~**TF-020H1-004**: rule-config disable canary missing~~ ✅ **closed in slice 020H.4** (this PR's branch). New `canary/rule-config-disabled` branch (PR #81 DO-NOT-MERGE; SHA `841d350`) carries the deliberate SCP-R-001 violation + a `.scp/rule-config.yaml` disable entry; workflow run `25211284467` verified PASS (deny suppressed by rule-config code path; findings=0; waivers=0; disabled_rules=2). `scripts/replay-canary.sh` registry extended with `rule-config-disabled|canary/rule-config-disabled|SUCCESS|0|0`. `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/canary-evidence.md` extended with Canary 4 baseline section. Suppression-path coverage triad complete: deny / waiver-suppressed / rule-config-suppressed.\n- ~~**TF-020H1-005**~~ ✅ primary deliverable closed in 020H.1 fix-round-1 (SAFE-nit-008): `RULE-TEMPLATE.md` §10 `[BLOCKING]` / `[deferrable]` question-marking guidance + no-quorum-with-unresolved-`[BLOCKING]` invariant landed. This TF remains nominally open only for any subsequent §10 enhancement (e.g. an auto-detect linter that flags unresolved `[BLOCKING]` markers in a proposal PR). No deadline (cosmetic).\n\n## Tracked-forward items from 020H.3 (release-gate)\n\n- **TF-020H3rg-001**: PR-time deprecation-announcement linter — currently a rule-deprecation PR adds an entry to `policies/deprecations.yaml` per the rule-RFC process; no automated check that the entry is added when a `deprecated` annotation is introduced. Closure path: a future linter step in `policy-check.yml` (or a separate workflow) that greps for new `deprecated` warning emissions in a PR diff and refuses the PR if no corresponding `policies/deprecations.yaml` entry was added in the same PR. No deadline (forward-compat). Filed at 020H.3 R1 completeness COMP-MIN-002 closure.\n- ~~**TF-020H3rg-002**: `pip install --require-hashes` for `policy-check.yml` + `release-gate.yml` pyyaml/jsonschema installs.~~ ✅ **closed in slice 020M** (this PR's branch). `requirements/policy-check.in` (top-level pins) + `requirements/policy-check.txt` (generated by `pip-compile --generate-hashes`, full transitive closure with all-platform wheel SHA256s) added. All 5 install sites (4× `policy-check.yml` + 1× `release-gate.yml`) switched to `pip install --require-hashes -r requirements/policy-check.txt`. Top-level pins unchanged from v1.0.0 (`pyyaml==6.0.2` + `jsonschema==4.23.0`); only the install mechanism is hardened. PATCH bump v1.0.0 → v1.0.1 per VERSIONING.md \"internal refactors\". D-038 filed.\n- ~~**TF-020H3rg-003**: Auto-open `release-gate-violation` issue on push:tags failure~~ ✅ **closed in slice 020H.3.1** (this PR's branch). `.github/workflows/release-gate.yml` split into two jobs: `release-gate` (evaluation; `contents: read`) + `release-gate-violation-issue` (`needs: release-gate`; `if: needs.release-gate.result == 'failure' && github.event_name == 'push'`; `permissions: { contents: read, issues: write }`; pre-creates labels via `gh label create --force`; de-dups by tag substring; uses Python templating in both new-issue and comment branches). Ratified by **D-037** (issues:write job-level scope). Forward-compat assignee env: `SCP_RELEASE_GATE_ASSIGNEES` (defaults to `jrnb2024`).\n- **TF-020H3rg-004**: Issue auto-close on corrective tag-cut — when the operator cuts the corrected `v<X>.<Y+1>.0`, the open `release-gate-violation` issue isn't auto-closed. Operator closes manually after the triage checklist completes. Closure path: a future workflow step that detects the corrected tag-cut and `gh issue close`s any open release-gate-violation issue for the bad tag-series. No deadline (forward-compat). Filed at 020H.3.1 R1 completeness COMP-MIN-001 closure.\n\n## Tracked-forward items from 020M (supply-chain hash-pinning)\n\n- ~~**TF-020M-001**: `conflict-gate.yml` retains `pip install pyyaml>=6.0` (line ~42) without hash-pinning.~~ ✅ **closed in slice 020N** (this PR's branch). `requirements/conflict-gate.in` (top-level pins matching `pyproject.toml` `[project.dependencies]` + `[project.optional-dependencies.dev]`) + `requirements/conflict-gate.txt` (generated by `pip-compile --generate-hashes` under Python 3.12, full transitive closure with all-platform wheel SHA256s) added. `.github/workflows/conflict-gate.yml` \"Install Python dependencies\" step restructured to: (i) hash-pinned `pip install --require-hashes -r requirements/conflict-gate.txt`; (ii) local vendored `ct-auth` wheel installed `--no-deps`; (iii) editable local SCP package installed `--no-deps`; (iv) post-install version-pin assertion (mirrors 020M SAFE-MAJ-002 pattern). No semver bump (conflict-gate is internal-only per VERSIONING.md §\"Scope\"). D-039 filed.\n- ~~**TF-020M-002**: ADOPT-001 §12.7.13 lockfile regeneration procedure does not warn that the hardcoded version-pin assertion strings must be updated in lockstep when bumping the lockfile.~~ ✅ **already inline-closed in slice 020M fix-round-2** (commit `37bbf5e`). The REGENERATION INVARIANT callout added to ADOPT-001 §12.7.13 explicitly names the four hardcoded `assert yaml.__version__ ==` / `assert jsonschema.__version__ ==` sites that must be updated in lockstep. The TF entry filed by the R2 safety reviewer was redundant with the inline closure; pruned in slice 020N STATUS.md update.\n\n## Tracked-forward items from 020N (conflict-gate hash-pinning)\n\n- **TF-020N-001**: `conflict-gate.yml` `permissions: id-token: write` is workflow-default scoped (line ~23) and applies across all steps including the new pip-install step (slice 020N). The `id-token: write` was originally added for `gh attestation verify` of OPA/Conftest binaries (a pre-020N step). With slice 020N's hash-pinned pip install above the attestation step, the `id-token: write` exposure surface during the pip-install network call is now broader than necessary — pip itself does not need OIDC. Closure path: narrow the privilege to job-level or step-level scoping so the new pip-install step runs with `contents: read` only. Forward-compat; symmetric posture with D-037's `release-gate-violation-issue` job-level scoping (slice 020H.3.1). Filed at 020N R1 safety SAFE-MIN-003 closure.\n\n## Tracked-forward items from 020L (first rule-RFC dogfood)\n\n- **TF-020L-001**: Unicode-whitespace regex divergence between Python `re` (Unicode-aware `\\S`) and OPA RE2 (ASCII-only `\\s`). For the §6.2 ASCII fixture corpus the divergence is irrelevant; a future fixture with Unicode whitespace in a URL-like string may surface conflict-gate flap. Closure path: Phase-2 implementation monitors SCP self-dogfood gate for `SCP-E005` flap on Unicode-whitespace input; if observed, anchor the regex pattern to ASCII-only printable range (e.g. `https?://[\\x21-\\x7e]+`) in both engines and add a fixture. Close as no-op if no divergence surfaces during the warn-baseline observation window. **Status at v1.1.0 cut (2026-05-02): no flap observed across slice 020P CI, release-gate dry-run, and post-tag observer; continue monitoring across estate adopters until ~30-90d post-v1.1.0.** Forward-compat; no deadline. Filed at 020L R1 correctness COR-NIT-001 closure.\n- ~~**TF-020L-002**: RULE-TEMPLATE.md §5 lacks residual-bypass guidance for rules enforcing syntactic-only patterns.~~ ✅ **closed in slice 020P** (PR #91, commit `d83ce52`); RULE-TEMPLATE.md §5 amended with \"Residual known bypass (for syntactic-pattern rules)\" guidance pointing at RULE-001 §5 case 5 as worked example.\n- ~~**TF-020L-003**: README.md §3 Merge says \"An entry in `docs/DECISIONS.md` if the rule introduces a new domain...\" but does NOT define \"new domain\".~~ ✅ **closed in slice 020P** (PR #91, commit `d83ce52`); README.md §3 amended with \"new domain\" definition (new top-level input schema OR no existing SCP-R-NNN counterpart; same-input-schema additions are same-domain).\n\n## Tracked-forward items from 020P (RULE-001 Phase 2)\n\n- **TF-020P-001**: data-driven `policies/rule-baselines.yaml` + `schemas/rule-baselines.schema.json` to replace the hardcoded `WARN_BASELINE_RULES = {\"SCP-R-004\"}` set in `.github/workflows/policy-check.yml`. Closure path: file when a 2nd warn-baseline rule lands (likely during the next rule-RFC slice). Hardcoded set is sufficient at v1.1.0 (single warn-baseline rule). Forward-compat; no deadline. Filed in DISPATCH-NOTE risk surface + release notes + workflow inline comment.\n- **TF-020P-002**: conflict-gate fixture corpus has 2 fixtures (1 allow + 1 deny) vs RULE-001 §6.2's spec'd ~12 (matches established SCP-R-001/002 minimal-smoke-test pattern; Conftest tests cover full corpus exhaustively). Closure path: EITHER expand conflict-gate fixture corpus to match RULE-001 §6.2 verbatim (10 more fixture pairs) OR amend RULE-TEMPLATE.md §6.2 framing to canonise the minimal-smoke-test pattern. Lightweight; foldable into next RFC slice or process-doc maintenance slice. Forward-compat; no deadline. Filed at 020P R1 completeness COMP-MIN-001 closure.\n- ~~**TF-020P-003**~~ ✅ **closed 2026-05-02 PM-4 in TF-020P-005 slice (this PR)** — absorbed by `scripts/scp-pre-push-verify.sh`'s Regal lint gate (parity with CI \"Lint policies with Regal\" step, same disable list).\n- ~~**TF-020P-004**~~ ✅ **closed 2026-05-02 PM-4 in TF-020P-005 slice (this PR)** — absorbed by `scripts/scp-pre-push-verify.sh`'s per-rule `opa test --coverage --threshold 90 --fail-on-empty -v` gate (parity with CI \"Enforce per-rule OPA coverage\" step).\n- ~~**TF-020P-005**~~ ✅ **closed 2026-05-02 PM-4 (this PR)** — `scripts/scp-pre-push-verify.sh` lands; ~150 lines bash, mirrors all three CI rule-author gates (Regal lint + `opa fmt --fail` + per-rule `opa test --coverage --threshold 90 --fail-on-empty -v`); aggregate failure collection; non-fatal `.tool-versions` parity warning; CODEOWNERS already covers via `scripts/** @jrnb2024`. ADOPT-001 §12.7.9.1 references the wrapper as recommended-not-required for rule authors.\n- **TF-020P-005b**: ADOPT-001 §12.7.9.1 audience-placement reorganisation. The wrapper section sits as a sub-section of §12.7.9 (adopter pre-commit hook section) but its audience is SCP-repo rule authors. Acceptable for v1.1.0 with the explicit \"Audience: SCP-repo rule authors only\" clarifier added in slice TF-020P-005 (this PR). Closure path: opportunistic next ADOPT-001 structural pass — move §12.7.9.1 to a dedicated §12.x SCP-self tooling section. Forward-compat; no deadline. Filed at TF-020P-005 R1 completeness COMP-MIN-001.\n- **TF-020P-005c**: optional `SCP_PRE_PUSH_VERSION_STRICT=1` env var to make `scripts/scp-pre-push-verify.sh`'s `.tool-versions` parity check fatal — for CI-in-CI or strict local-dev workflows where version drift should hard-fail. Default behaviour stays non-fatal warning per slice 020P-005 design (DISPATCH-NOTE Risk #1). Closure path: opportunistic; file when a second requestor surfaces the need. Forward-compat; no deadline. Filed at TF-020P-005 R1 completeness COMP-NIT-003.\n\n## Tracked-forward items from WP-SCP-023 023A (plan-doc) + 023B (emitter) + 023C (aggregator)\n\n- **TF-023A-001** (low priority): R-023-01 k-anonymity mitigation framing clarification when WP-SCP-024 cascade slice begins. The plan-doc R-023-01 risk row references \"slice 024 introduces aggregator-side k-anonymity\"; tighten when WP-SCP-024 plan-doc lands. Forward-compat; opportunistic.\n- **TF-023A-002** (medium priority): Cross-repo notification (v1.2.0 release announcement to ACC / CT / mapp-estate-regression) — **re-deferred to slice 023E** (was 023D; 023D ships exposure surface but Threshold A onboarding is where adopters first participate). Until adopters can opt in with the exposure surface live, the notification is a \"pre-Threshold-A FYI\" only. Filed at WP-SCP-023 023A; re-deferred at 023D R1 completeness CMP-MIN-001.\n- **TF-023B-001** (low priority): Workflow-selftest harness `fixture-pass-with-scorecard-emit` — extend `tests/workflow/fixture-pass/` to cover the new opt-in `scorecard-emit: true` input on the SCP self-dogfood wrapper. Target slice 023C (when SCP self-dogfood wrapper is extended with `scorecard-emit: true` to feed the aggregator's first run). Forward-compat. Filed at 023B R1 completeness CG-MIN-005.\n- **TF-023B-002** (low priority): FLA-pilot canary scorecard fixture — capture FLA's first successful scorecard emit at slice 023E as a permanent fixture. Target slice 023E. Filed at 023B R1 completeness CG-nit-003.\n- **TF-023B-003** (low priority): Promote `WARN_BASELINE_RULES` to data-driven manifest per TF-020P-001's scope. Filed at 023B R3 R3-MIN-SAFE-002.\n- **TF-023C-001** (medium priority): SCP self-dogfood — opt the SCP repo's own `policy-check-wrapper.yml` self-test into `scorecard-emit: true` so the aggregator has a 1-adopter test corpus before real adopters arrive. Target slice 023E (or earlier).\n- **TF-023C-002** (low priority): cron-health monitor — alert when `scorecard-aggregator.yml` hasn't produced a fresh index in >2 weeks. Target slice 023E or post-Threshold-A maintenance.\n- **TF-023C-003** (low priority): rate-limit handling for large estate. Filed at 023C R1 completeness CG-nit-002.\n- **TF-023C-004** (low priority): aggregator job `timeout-minutes` constraint. Filed at 023C R1 safety nit-SAFE-004.\n\n---\n| D-032 | 2026-04-30 | Apply WP-SCP-020 slice 020D2 on the SCP repository post-USER-GATE-A0: enable `scp/policy-check` as a required status check on `main` with `strict: true` (PR must be up-to-date with base before evaluation); set `enforce_admins: true` (no admin bypass); set `required_pull_request_reviews` with `required_approving_review_count: 1`, `dismiss_stale_reviews: true`, `require_code_owner_reviews: true`; explicitly leave `require_review_from_non_author: false` per 020K personal-account closure (single-operator self-approval is the only viable path). Configured via `scripts/configure-020d2-required-check.sh` (idempotent). After 020D2, every PR to `main` must pass the federation primitive's gate AND have at least one approving review AND have a verified signature on every commit AND cannot be bypassed by the admin role. The 020E.a pre-protection canary (workflow-run-id 25172373569) demonstrated the deny path on a real PR with a real violation pre-flip; 020E.b will demonstrate that the now-required check actually blocks merge. Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: a single GitHub admin (@jrnb2024) is the operator; quarterly review at 2026-07-21 (per 020K + D-031) reconciles documented-vs-live state. **Note (D-033 forward-reference, 2026-04-30 evening):** the live state of three D-032 parameters was amended same-day by D-033 — the required-check context name corrected from `scp/policy-check` to `policy-check / scp/policy-check` (rendered Actions name); `required_approving_review_count` corrected from 1 to 0 (single-operator self-approval is structurally impossible on GitHub); `require_code_owner_reviews` corrected from true to false (same root cause). See D-033 for the operational test path that surfaced these | ACCEPTED | This is the operational closure of the WP-SCP-020 federation primitive — SCP gates itself on its own `main`. Closure of governance B-2 (the original brief was \"convert SCP from advisory auditor to deterministic pre-merge enforcement\"). Required-status-check + enforce_admins=true + required-signed-commits + required-PR-reviews compose into a 4-layer protection: (1) every commit is cryptographically attested, (2) every change runs through the SCP gate, (3) every change has at least one human approval, (4) admin override is OFF. Single-operator self-approval is the bus-factor-1 cost; the 2026-07-21 escalation review is the named re-evaluation moment. The pre-protection canary (020E.a) proved the deny mechanism worked on real PR; flipping to required adds enforcement, not behaviour. Identified at WP-SCP-020 plan §3 sequence + §4 020D2; preconditions 020J + 020K + 020D1 + 020E.a + USER-GATE-A0 all closed before this slice opens |\n| D-033 | 2026-04-30 | WP-SCP-022 020D2.1 reconciliation: amend D-032's branch-protection shape on the SCP repo to reflect two operational realities surfaced when the first PR (USER-GATE-A signoff PR #64) attempted to merge through enforced mode. (a) **Required-check context name correction:** WP-SCP-020 020B(xi) specified `scp/policy-check` as the context name. GitHub Actions renders the actual check-run as `<wrapper-workflow-name> / <reusable-job-name>` — for SCP self this is `policy-check / scp/policy-check`. The bare `scp/policy-check` context matches only the readback status posted by the reusable workflow's commit-status step, NOT the primary check-run from the wrapper. Required-check context updated to `policy-check / scp/policy-check`. (b) **Personal-account review-shape correction:** D-032 originally set `required_approving_review_count = 1` + `require_code_owner_reviews = true` per WP-SCP-020 020D2 spec. GitHub forbids PR authors from approving their own PRs. In single-operator mode with @jrnb2024 as the only maintainer AND only CODEOWNER, count=1 + codeowner=true locks the operator out of every PR; `enforce_admins=true` prevents `gh pr merge --admin` from bypassing. Updated to `count=0` + `codeowner_reviews=false` in single-operator mode. CODEOWNERS still serves as documentation of who SHOULD approve when a second maintainer arrives. Forward-looking discipline preserved: when a second maintainer onboards, flip count=1 + codeowner=true + non-author=true in one operation. Both corrections are landed in `scripts/configure-020d2-required-check.sh` (idempotent re-run reproduces the live state) + `docs/security/branch-protection.md` + WP-SCP-020 §8 risk row. The 2026-07-21 quarterly escalation review re-evaluates the personal-account shape | ACCEPTED | First-PR-through-enforcement is the operational test of the spec; the test surfaced two assumptions that didn't survive contact with GitHub's actual behaviour: (1) the bare context name from 020B(xi) was incomplete (didn't anticipate Actions' `<workflow> / <job>` rendering for reusable-workflow callers), and (2) \"self-approval is the only option\" in 020K's wording was operationally impossible (GitHub forbids PR self-review). Both corrections are operational closure of the spec gap; neither weakens the security posture. The 4-layer protection (signed commits + required check + no admin bypass + tag protection) remains intact. The review-count=0 acceptance is the explicit bus-factor-1 cost; review enforcement returns the moment a second maintainer joins. Identified by USER-GATE-A signoff PR #64's failed merge attempt 2026-04-30 |\n| D-034 | 2026-04-30 | Apply WP-SCP-020 slice 020F renovate-tag-protection (parallel ruleset to D-030's `v*` ruleset, targeting `refs/tags/renovate/v*`). Closes 020F R1 safety review CRIT-SAFE-001: `renovate/v*` tag series unprotected — an attacker with push access could silently re-point `renovate/v1.0.0` to a malicious commit and cascade adversarial Renovate config to every estate adopter on their next scheduled run. The 020J ruleset matches `refs/tags/v*` (literal v-prefix at start) only. New ruleset `scp-tag-protection-renovate-v` applies same protections (deletion / non_fast_forward / update blocked, `enforcement: active`, `bypass_actors: []`). Configured via `scripts/configure-020f-renovate-tag-protection.sh` (idempotent, jq-based JSON construction to eliminate heredoc-interpolation injection surface, multi-property post-creation verification). Documented in `docs/security/branch-protection.md` \"Tag protection — renovate/v* pattern\" section. Symmetric with D-030 in posture and rationale; the only material difference is the tag-pattern segment. The `renovate/v*` series carries equal supply-chain weight as `v*` because every adopter that extends the preset cascades changes from the renovate-pattern tag to their own gate config | ACCEPTED | The 020J ruleset's `v*` literal-prefix pattern is by-design narrow; broadening to all release-track tags would require a separate ruleset per pattern. Renovate's preset shorthand `github>jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-//renovate/default#renovate/v1.0.0` is the standard Renovate adopter onboarding shape; without ruleset protection, the entire preset trust chain is rooted in mutable tag refs. Bus-factor-1 acknowledged identically to D-030: the same admin who owns @jrnb2024 is the one publishing tags; the protection guards against accidental force-push, not against malicious admin action. Quarterly review cadence (2026-07-30 in STATUS.md \"Open scheduled follow-ups\") covers both rulesets together. Identified by 020F R1 safety review (workflow run dispatched 2026-04-30 evening) — surfaced under the no-silent-descope governance invariant after fix-round-1 closed the substantive R1 findings |\n| D-035 | 2026-04-30 | Adopt the WP-SCP-020 slice 020G adopter-helper invocation procedure as estate doctrine. The required-check context name `policy-check / scp/policy-check` traces to D-033 (the rendered Actions check-run name established for the SCP self-dogfood gate). Adopters of the SCP federation primitive enable this required status check on their default branch via `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` from the SCP repo. The script applies branch protection in two API calls (unified PUT for status-checks/admins/reviews + dedicated POST to `required_signatures` sub-resource per the GitHub API shape), refuses to bypass admin enforcement without an explicit `--i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate` acknowledgement flag, refuses to run in CI (CI=true / GITHUB_ACTIONS=true env-var guards), preserves any pre-existing `required_pull_request_reviews` shape rather than nulling it, and emits an invocation-log block (operator, timestamp, script SHA256 + git SHA, target repo+branch, before/after API JSON) for paste into `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md`. The log commit is part of the invocation procedure: an apply without the log entry is considered unrecorded. Estate cascade rollout (WP-SCP-024) drives this script across PIM, recommender, shopify-app, mapp-doc-agent, control-tower; FLA pilot (WP-SCP-020.1) is the canary first invocation | ACCEPTED | Symmetric posture with D-030 (020J `v*` tag-protection), D-031 (020K CODEOWNERS personal-account), D-032 (020D2 SCP-self required-status-check), D-034 (020F `renovate/v*` tag-protection): every operational procedure that mutates third-party repository state ships an idempotent applier + ratifying D-NNN + invocation log convention. The bootstrap-only / no-CI guard reflects that this script writes to a third-party repo's branch protection — an automation tool that ran it unattended could mass-mutate the estate via stolen credentials before any operator noticed. The `--i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate` confirmation reflects that `--no-enforce-admins` defeats the whole point of the federation primitive on the target repo and so should require explicit intent. The `required_pull_request_reviews` preservation reflects that adopters with multi-maintainer teams have legitimate review-shape state that 020G must not destroy. Identified at WP-SCP-020 §4 020G + 020G R1 review (3 MAJ + 5 MIN + 2 nit on safety, 2 MAJ + 4 MIN + nit on completeness, 3 MAJ + 2 MIN + 2 nit on correctness — fixpoint via fix-round-1) |\n| D-036 | 2026-05-01 | Adopt `policies/VERSIONING.md` MAJOR/MINOR/PATCH semver contract on the SCP federation primitive's public surfaces (`workflow